 "words": {
  "rule": "Posted streets are swept every other week, on the 1st and 3rd or the 2nd and 4th time that weekday comes in the month: one side of the street on one day, the other side on another, during the hours on the sign.",
  "afterpass": "All year. No sweeping on City holidays, and no make-up day. $73 ticket, no tow.",
  "dataNotes": "Days, weeks and hours come from StreetsLA's posted sweeping routes. StreetsLA doesn't publish which side of the street is swept on which day, so CURB placed the 900,142 street cleaning tickets written since January 2025 on their block and side by address, and gave each side the day its tickets fall on; a block with no tickets takes the side of the nearest ticketed block on its street. Where neither tells, both days show on both sides."
 },
